  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "Use lean beef or horse meat. Remove fat and connective tissue before grinding. Mix meat, water and NaOH, then boil for 15 min with stirring."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Cool to room temperature, skim fat off surface, and filter, retaining both meat particles and filtrate."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "To the filtrate add water to a final volume of 1000 ml, and then add:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "To make medium anoxic bring it to a boil, cool under 100% N2 gas atmosphere, add 0.5 g/l L-cysteine hydrochloride and adjust pH to 7.0."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "Dispense under 100% N2 gas atmosphere by filling 7 ml medium into anoxic Hungate-type tubes (for strains demanding meat particles put those first into the tube (use 1 part meat particles to 4 or 5 parts fluid))."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "Autoclave at 121oC for 30 min. For agar slants use 15.0 g agar per 1000.0 ml medium."
    }
  ]
}